## Course overview

German B at Standard Level is a language-acquisition course for students with prior experience of German. The emphasis is on **communication in real contexts** — understanding and producing spoken and written German across a range of registers — organised around five prescribed themes: *identities, experiences, human ingenuity, social organisation,* and *sharing the planet*.

## What you will study

- The five themes through authentic texts: articles, interviews, blogs, and literature extracts.
- Receptive skills (listening and reading), productive skills (writing and speaking), and interaction.
- Grammar and vocabulary in service of fluent, accurate communication.

## Assessment

| Component | Weighting | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 | 25% | Productive writing |
| Paper 2 | 50% | Listening + reading comprehension |
| Individual Oral | 25% | Discussion based on a visual stimulus |

## The Individual Oral

The **Individual Oral** begins with a description of a photograph linked to one of the themes, followed by a conversation. It assesses spontaneous communication, range, and accuracy — the everyday ability to use German with confidence.
